<newsitem itemid="57017" id="root" date="1996-09-16" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Travis Perkins H1 pretax profits edge up.</title>
<headline>Travis Perkins H1 pretax profits edge up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.2		   vs 10.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.0		    vs 2.8</p>
<p> Pretax		     17.22		  vs 16.91</p>
<p> Turnover		   249.67		 vs 242.85</p>
<p>NOTE - UK timber and building materials group Travis Perkins Plc said housing starts continued to fall throughout the first half of 1996. But it added that mortgage approvals and housing transactions had all increased, offering &quot;some encouragement&quot; for the future.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 16.52		  vs 17.06</p>
<p> Exceptional charges    1.49		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   0.13 receivable    vs 0.18 payable</p>
<p> Tax charge		 5.65		   vs 5.85</p>
<p> Net taxed		  11.56		  vs 11.07</p>
<p> Retained		   8.45		   vs 8.18</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 1</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 8</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Sept 30</p>
<p>NOTE - The exceptional charge was for reorganisation costs.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
